# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings.
#
# Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, which turned every script
# into CRLF — bash then dies on the shebang/`set` lines (`$'\r': command not
# found`, `set: pipefail: invalid option name`), so `bun run check:rust` never
# actually ran a check.
*.sh text eol=lf
